    <span id="page-body"></span>
    <div id="maincontent2" class="article" role="main"> <!-- InstanceBeginEditable name="maincontent2" -->
      <h1>Labor Law Publications </h1>
      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Summary: <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/llupdates/2025/index.shtml" target="_blank">2025</a> | <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/llupdates/2023/index.shtml" target="_blank">2023</a> | <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/llupdates/2022/index.shtml" target="_blank">2022</a> | <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/llupdates/2021/index.shtml" target="_blank">2021</a> | <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/llupdates/2020/index.shtml" target="_blank">2020</a> | <a href="/labor/labor_laws/llupdates/2019/index.shtml" target="_blank">2019</a> | <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/2017_labor_laws.html" target="_blank">2017</a> | <a href="2016_labor_laws.html">2016</a> | <a href="2015_labor_laws.html">2015</a> | <a href="2014_labor_laws.html">2014</a> | <a href="2013_labor_laws.html">2013</a> | <a href="2012_labor_laws.html">2012</a> | <a href="2011_labor_laws.html">2011</a> | <a href="https://www.maine.gov/tools/whatsnew/index.php?topic=Labor+Press+Releases&amp;id=113952&amp;v=Article">2010</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/posters/index.shtml" target="_blank">Maine Labor Posters</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>The following links provide information and resources concerning Maine employment laws, many of which are enforced by the Maine Department of Labor, Wage and Hour Division.</p>
     
      <div class="row">
        <div class="column">
    
          <h3>Child Labor</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26ch7sec0.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes (Go to Sub-chapter 4, Article 3)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/publications/minorsguide.shtml" target="_blank">Guide to Maine Laws Governing the Employment of Minors</a></li>
            <li><a href="../docs/2022/laborlaws/HazardousOccupationsRules.pdf"
target="_blank">Hazardous Occupations Rules</a> (PDF)</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/posters/index.shtml" target="_blank">Child Labor Poster</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/26/title26sec775.html" target="_blank">Work Permits Law</a></li>
            <li><a href="publications/2018/work_permit_072018.pdf" target="_blank">Download Maine Work Permit Form</a> (PDF)</li>
            <li><a href="../docs/2022/laborlaws/AgeVerificationform042022.pdf" target="_blank">Download Age Verification Form</a>&nbsp;(PDF) </li>
            <li><a href="/labor/docs/2024/laborlaws/EmployersGuidetoYouthEmployment.pdf" target="_blank">Employers  Guide to Youth Employment</a> (PDF)</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Earned Paid Leave</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/earnedpaidleave/" target="_blank">Earned Paid Leave Information</a></li>
            <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/statutes/26/title26sec637-2.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Employment Leave for Victims of Violence</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/cec/rules/12/170/170c010.docx"
target="_blank">Rules Relating to Employment Leave for Victims of Violence</a> (Word)</li>
            <li><a href="../labor_stats/publications/dvreports/domesticoffendersreport.pdf">Report on the Impact of Domestic Violence Offenders on Occupational Safety &amp; Health: A Pilot Study</a> (PDF)</li>
            <li><a href="../labor_stats/publications/dvreports/survivorstudy.pdf">Report on Domestic Violence Survivors at Work: How Perpetrators Impact Employment</a> (PDF)</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Equal Pay</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/labor/docs/2021/laborlaws/2021 Equal Pay Report 03.10.21.pdf" target="_blank">2021 Equal Pay Report</a> (PDF)</li>
            <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec628.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/cec/rules/12/170/170c012.doc"
target="_blank">Rules Relating to Equal Pay</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/publications/epcomplaintform.pdf" target="_blank">Equal Pay Complaint Form</a> (PDF)</li>
            <li>Equal Pay Self-Audit Tool For Employers (<a href="publications/epaudit.doc"
target="_blank">Word)</a> (<a href="publications/epaudit.pdf"
target="_blank">PDF)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/docs/2022/posters/equalpay_new.pdf" target="_blank">Equal Pay Poster</a> (PDF)</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Family Medical Leave</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec844.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a> (go to section 6-A) </li>
            <li><a href="https://webapps.dol.gov/elaws/fmla.htm" target="_blank">Federal Family Medical Leave Law</a></li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Final Payment of Wages</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec626.html"
target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
            <li>Interpretive Guidance relating to the payout of accrued vacation time (<a href="/labor/docs/2022/laborlaws/BLSInterpretiveGuidancePolicy22-01.docx" target="_blank">Word</a>) (<a href="/labor/docs/2022/laborlaws/BLSInterpretiveGuidancePolicy22-01.pdf" target="_blank">PDF</a>)</li>
            <li><a href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec632.html" target="_blank">Wage Assurance Fund Statutes</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/cec/rules/12/170/170c003.doc">Wage Assurance Fund Rules</a> (Word)</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Foreign Workers</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="hiring_foreign_workers.html">Visit the Migrant and Immigrant Services Website</a></li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Independent Contractors</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/misclass/employmentstandard/index.shtml" target="_blank">Independent Contractor vs. Employee: What you Need to Know</a><a href="publications/indcontrbro.pdf"></a> <a href="Independent Contractor vs. Employee: What you Need to Know"></a></li>
            <li><a href="publications/misclass.doc">Report on Misclassification of Workers in the Construction Industry</a> (Word)       </li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Minimum Pay for Reporting to Work</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="../docs/2025/laborlaws/wagehour/LD598Minimumpayforreportingtowork.pdf" target="_blank">Relevant Statute</a> (PDF)</li>
               <li><a href="../docs/2025/laborlaws/wagehour/NEWMinimumPayforReportingtoWorkguidance.pdf" target="_blank">Guidance</a> (PDF)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
  <div class="column">
    
    <h3>Minimum Wage &amp; Overtime</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="minwagehistory.html">History of Maine's Minimum Wage</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec603.html"
target="_blank">Limits on Mandatory Overtime</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/posters/index.shtml" target="_blank">Minimum Wage Poster</a></li>
      <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec664.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
      <li><a href="/labor/docs/2021/laborlaws/Salaried Workers Guidance rev 09.27.2021.pdf" target="_blank">Salaried Worker Guidance: A guideline to overtime requirements</a> (PDF)</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/docs/2019/laborlaws/minimumwage112019.pdf" target="_blank"></a><a href="../docs/2022/laborlaws/SalaryRules.pdf"
target="_blank">Salary vs. Hourly Test: Rules Governing Definitions for Executive, Administrative, and Professional Exemptions from Minimum Wage and Overtime</a> (PDF)</li>
      </ul>
    <h3>Prevailing Wage on State Construction Projects</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/statutes/26/title26ch15sec0.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
      <li><a href="../labor_stats/publications/wagerateconst/index.html"
target="_blank">Current Construction Wage Rates</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/cec/rules/12/170/170c013.doc"
target="_blank">Rules Relating to Fair Minimum Wage in Construction</a></li>
      <li><a href="/labor/docs/2020/laborstats/2020OccupationalCodes.pdf" target="_blank">Occupational Codes</a> (PDF)</li>
      </ul>
    <h3>Rest Breaks</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec601.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Safety</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="../workplace_safety/publicsector.shtml">Visit the Public Sector Safety Enforcement Website</a></li>
      <li><a href="http://www.safetyworksmaine.gov/" target="_blank">Visit the SafetyWorks! Website</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.osha.gov" target="_blank">Visit the OSHA Website</a></li>
      </ul>
    <h3>Severance Pay</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26sec625-B.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/cec/rules/12/170/170c015.doc">Severance Pay Rules</a></li>
      </ul>
    <h3><strong>Sexual Harassment</strong></h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="../docs/2026/laborlaws/MaineBLSSexualHarassmentPreventionChecklist.pdf" target="_blank">Sexual Harassment Training Checklist</a> (PDF)</li>
      <li><a href="/labor/posters/2017/sexual_harassment_poster.pdf" target="_blank">Sexual Harassment Training Poster</a> (PDF)</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Substance Use Testing</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a
href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26ch7sec0.html" target="_blank">Relevant Statutes (See Subchapter 3-A</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/substanceusetesting/"
target="_blank">Model Substance Abuse Testing Policy and Reports</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/cec/rules/12/170/170c007.doc"
target="_blank">Rules Relating to Substance Abuse Testing</a></li>
      <li>Study of Employer Attitudes Toward Substance Abuse and Substance Abuse Testing Programs in Maine: <a
href="../labor_stats/publications/substanceabuse/substanceabuseemployers.pdf">Adobe PDF version</a>, <a
href="../labor_stats/publications/substanceabuse/substanceabuseemployers.doc">MS Word version</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Unfair Agreements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a
href="https://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/26/title26sec629.html">Related Statutes</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>The Wage and Hour Division also:</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Consults on related labor laws</li>
      <li>Provides speakers on wage and hour issues</li>
      <li>Provides <a href="../posters/index.html" target="_blank">Required Labor Posters</a></li>
      <li>Publishes <a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/employeerightsguide/"
target="_blank">Maine Employee Rights Guide</a> and <a
href="publications/minorsguide.html" target="_blank">Guide to Maine Laws Governing the Employment of Minors</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/26/title26ch7sec0.html"
target="_blank">Title 26 Chapter 7</a> Maine laws governing employment practices</li>
      <li><a href="https://me-newhire.com/" target="_blank">New Hire Reporting</a> is a process by which you, as an employer, report information on newly-hired employees to us within 7 days of the date of hire.  </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
